To: "Peter M. Juhl" <pmj@dat.dtu.dk>
Organization: Univ. of Genoa, Italy
Newsgroups: comp.unix.osf.osf1


Dear Peter,

I had the same problem on my 433au. Digital suggested this fix, which
actually worked:

dbx -k /vmunix
assign db_enable = 0
quit

dbx /vmunix
patch db_enable = 0
quit

in this way we modify the running version of the kernel and the kernel
file on disk. If you do not want to do this every time you rebuild the
kernel you must also comment out the line containing KDEBUG in the file
/sys/config

if I understood correctly DU4.0c has some "minor problems" and so the
kernel is compiled in some debug mode which prevents the debugger to
debug user-code

Hope this helps,

Pier



