We have some au-series personal workstations running 4.0c, and
although I've not encountered the problem you describe, I have
seen a number of situations where, when we have two processes
which *are* CPU hogs (i.e. long computationally-intense jobs),
"top" will show both of them with >98% of a CPU, or just under
100% for one job and just under 50% for the other.

I *know* there's only one CPU in those boxes.  (At any rate,
that's what we've been told.  But if they're really dual-CPU
machines, I'll be pleasantly surprised. ;-)

So I've been wondering whether this is a bug in the current
version of "top", or whether whatever kernel information is
being used by top is being reported erroneously (i.e. "top"
is OK, but the kernel is misinforming it).

PS:  And, to avoid the obvious question:  Yes, I did rebuild
"top" for this version of DUnix.

