For five instances you should have at least 512 MB of memory.
Probably you need to redesign your databases in one instance.
For one instance you need shared memory:
shmmax = 4194304
shmseg = 32

ORACLE's SGA may be no larger than the value:
shmmax * shmseg * 8192

One instance - it may be 6-26 processes without user' access,
according to your init.ora parameters.

For multiple instances you need to increase next parameters:
maxusers - number of simultaneous users that your system can
	   support without straining system resources
nclist - number of clists available on the system
max_vnodes - max number of VFS files
task_max - set a limit on the number of processes that can be running
	   on the system
maxuprc - maximum number of processes for one user (ALL YOU INSTANCES
	  STARTING BY ONE USER - ORACLE)
(See "System Administration" book: 5-37 - 5-42)

dfldsiz, maxdsiz, dflssuz, and maxssiz - stay in peace

Regards!
