DEC your driving me crazy !

It seems that every 6 - 12 months DEC changes their Graphics Subsystem for
AlphaStations and Servers.  Forget the "cute" marketing names.  First we
had the PBXGA-Ax/Bx/Cx series (the ZLXp-E1/2/3).  Then we had the PBXGC-xx
(ZLXp-L1/2) series.  And don't forget the PB2GA-xx/PBXGB-xx/PBXGI-xx
(PowerStorm 3D10/3D30/4D20/4D40) variants.

The problem is certain Graphic Subsystems are only "supported" on certain
models of AlphaStations and Servers, even though (to the best of my
knowledge) these all have PCI bus interfaces.  Some stations/servers
"require" certain suffix versions that I have never even seen !!!

For example, I have several Alphastation 200 and 400's with PBXGA-AA
Graphics Subsystems.  I want to add another Graphics Subsystem to support
two monitors.  These boards are no longer available (according to the
Electronic Store).  The PB2GA-JC/JD which are available, aren't supported
in multiscreen configurations.  I guess I'll have to buy the PBXGB-AA, but
can I mix PBXGA-AA and PBXGB-AA on the same system ?

The Alphastation 255's I bought 12 months ago with dual PBXGA-BA Graphics
Subsystems are not even officially "supported" under DUNIX V4.0 !

Finally, why is the AlphaServer 2100A 5/300 "limited" to the anemic PB2GA
!!!  And what is the difference between PB2GA-JA/JB (which is supported but
not available) and the PB2GA-JC/JD (which is not supported but IS
available) ????

Come on DEC, why can't all PCI bused Alpha's use all of "your" PCI bus
Graphics Subsystems ??!!!!!

Jack Patteeuw

