I have an older version of CAP running on DU 4.0B.  It survived the
upgrade from 3.2C without any difficulties.
We are not certain what the patch level of the previous installation
was.   Regardless, compiling of CAP patchlevel 198 fails on this machine
now.  (The same failures are present when the new appleshare-ip patch is
applied -- which is why I'm really doing this update.)

1. in printqueue.c there is an error caused by a pointer, "readdir"
which is of type "struct dirent" which is not compatible with type
"struct direct."  There is a warning about d->d_name being a member of
another
structure.  There are also two unresolved references:

            OSLockFileForRead
            OSUnlockFile

2. in building aufs, there is a problem compiling afpos.c  because of
the same incompatibility of structures as in #1
    above and the same warnings about d_name.   "aufs" is not produced.

3. in building support/ethertalk, compiling of snitp.c fails because it
can't find <net/nit.h>


If we're only using phase 2 native ethernet do we need support/ethertalk
at all?
Anyone have fixes to these problems?

