}a hard lockup of the system, ending in a machine check.
}

That particular problem (on the 255) isn't related to Netscape per se - you
can also trigger it by displaying some of the background bitmaps provided with
CDE.  DEC tech support had me load newer video drivers for that card that
come in a subset of their Open3D product - that fixed it. The subset is:

O3DDWSZLXE400        installed  DWS Open3D ZLX-E, ZLXp-E, PowerStorm 3D30,
                                PowerStorm 4D20 V4.0

There are also drivers for other cards in the Open3D bundle. We don't have
any ZLX cards in TurboChannel machines, so I can't tell you whether it will
fix the problem on the DEC3000/500 as well.

