> open: ln0: Permission denied
> NBPInit: DDPOpenSocket error 13
> papif: Starting job for root@otto.med.harvard.edu at Thu Aug 21 15:24:00
> 1997 on printer cf522:LaserWriter@EQRF
> NBP nbpFcn: nbpInit not called>>
> Filter 'f' terminated (sig=-1,err=1)
> <<

CAP on Digital Unix requires:
1. Kernel packetfilter support to be enabled (RTFM packetfilter)
2. Packetfilter device files to be created (cd /dev; ./MAKEDEV pfilt)

Furthermore, papif requires write permissons on /dev/pf/pfilt*. This
can be accomplished by either making papif setuid or setgid.

/Erik

