Mark Bartelt wrote:
> 
> Sorry to bother you all once again, but now I have yet another
> question on the topic of the v4.0c CD.  And this one may need
> the expertise of Tom Blinn, or someone equally savvy ...
> 
> Suppose that I use the v4.0c CD to do a fresh installation on
> something other than an au-series PW, so v4.0b gets installed.
> Now I want to install the latest ftp.service.digital.com patch
> kit.
> 
> Do I use the 4.0b patch kit (v4.0b/duv40bas00004-19970808.tar),
> since the system itself is really v4.0b?  Or should I be using
> the 4.0c patch kit (v4.0c/duv40cas00001-19970603.tar) since the
> installation was done from a 4.0c CD?
> 

The V4.0C kit contains complete V4.0B and V4.0C kits on it and
when you install this kit on any older hardware the results is
identical to installing the V4.0B kit only.

When you install this kit on a the new hardware it will install
the V4.0B kit and then add the new files to support the new
hardware.

For applying patches, you should only install the V4.0B patches
on a V4.0B system and the V4.0C patches on a V4.0C system because
you can get the kernel hardware support out of sync and possibly
not be able to boot the system.

Sean



