Terrence Brannon <brannon@quake.usc.edu> writes:
> But when I attempt mount /dev/rrz5c /jaz
>
> It says "Block device needed"

Right.  /dev/rrz5c is not a block device, it's a character device.  You need
to do:

mount /dev/rz5c /jaz

Note the single "r" after /dev/, instead of the double "rr".  The extra "r"
in the character device name stands for "raw".
