Robert Moniot wrote:
> 
> Lately some of our users have been generating zombie processes.  These
> are processes that ps calls "defunct", i.e.  a process that has exited
> but whose parent process has not waited for it.  The parent process is
> either 1 (init) or another defunct process whose parent is 1.  Trying
> to kill these defunct processes gives the message "no such process",
> but they continue to tie up tty's.  (These particular ones are on LAT
> tty's, of which we have defined a limited number.)  Is there any way
> to clear these zombies out of the process table other than rebooting?
> 
> We are running OSF1 V4.0 on an AlphaStation 1000.

Terminate the parent processes; once they are gone the zombies will be
cleaned up by the init process (PID = 0).

This is an inherent feature of Unix in general (*not* just DU). It shows
that someone has not designed an application well!

