The old Adaptec chip on Jensens has timing that is RIGHT at the hairy
edge of not working. That's why it gets pushed out of timing when
the bus gets too long. And Adaptec doesn't make that chip any more,
so there's no fix from the manufacturer. 

The upshot is that on a Jensen using the Adaptec board, keep the
SCSI bus REAL short. Running things slowly may also keep from getting
outside timing.

A SCSI bus that is too long has lots of problems, particularly when
more than one device thinks it won arbitration for the bus at one
time. Hangs and worse are easy to get.

A 9GB disk is likely to be more demanding in its SCSI timing than
older gadgets.



