M�ri Peter wrote:

> I am running 10 DEC3000 Alphas under DU 3.2G, all the same
> applications.
> On Six of these, doing  "ps aux" they show a growing Xdec, and
> eventually
> I run out of Memory. After a Week I get 100Meg of Xdec.
>
> Any Idea?
>  Thanks
>         Peter


--

Have a look at 'man Xdec' and use the option '-terminate'. You have to
specify this in the
'/usr/lib/X11/Xserver.conf' file. This is the typical entry among the
others in this file, this is for
Digital Unix 4.0 - do not know for DU3.x but it is similar:

! you specify command line arguments here
!
! Joe - put '-terminate' argument in
args <
        -pn
        -terminate
>

I believe the reason why your Xdec process eventually uses a lot of
memory is that whenever a
XDM session is started it allocated new memory for it. When you exit the
XDM session Xdec does
not throw it away but keeps the baggage. Using the '-terminate' command
arg does actually free this.

Hope this helps

Joe Spanicek
joe@resptk.bhp.com.au




