Mark Fisher wrote:
> 
> Let me know what you find out. We have been experiencing this problem
> for a year running V4.0A and V4.0B. The df command never seems to
> display the correct free space. Sometimes we see 107% utilized!!!
> 
107% is possible! The df command shows the amount of space available to
normal (non-root) users. Unix file systems become inefficient once they
get to about 90% utilisation of the available disk partition space (I
don't know why, something about the file system structure), so typically
a file system is set so that users can only utilise 90% of the
partition.
BUT, root is not subject to this restriction, so root can create files
even when other users are blocked; when this happens df shows >100%
file system utilisation.

Under a normal configuration, a completely full file system (using all
of
the available partition space) will show as 110% on df! When this
happens,
system admins start to sweat.

Alan

